      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3a786be_bbc81267",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1093,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-17T04:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Long-ish run we\u0027ll have to revisit the idea of whether we want to keep the flag for discover being done, and when to set it.  It saves us running through our full discovery checklist every ready run, but is also redundant information. \n\nIt might also be worth breaking into SOP done and SOP\u0027 done when we do notifications, since we could potentially end up with a partner which won\u0027t allow us to discover one or the other (ex. if we can\u0027t swap to vconn source), but the kernel would still be capable of acting on the info we did collect (really, entering DP most likely).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1093,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 1093,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
